<title>USA: Shared Technologies named in lawsuit.</title>
<headline>Shared Technologies named in lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>WETHERSFIELD, Conn. 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shared Technologies Fairchild  Inc on Friday said it has been served with what it believes is a class-action  complaint by shareholders.</p>
<p>The lawsuit was filed in Delaware Chancery Court in New Castle County,  it said. Shared Technologies Fairchild and its directors are named  as defendants, the company said.</p>
<p>The company said the complaint seeks injunctive relief, costs, and  attorneys' fees with respect to its proposed merger with Tel-Save  Holdings Inc, which was announced on July 17.</p>
<p>Shared Technologies Fairchild, which provides services to tenants  of shared office buildings, said it thought the suit was without merit  and intended to defend itself vigorously.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
